# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY called node_modules and nothing else. A
# symlink called node_modules — which is what a linked local dependency is, and
# what several package managers create — is not a directory, so the pattern
# misses it and the link gets committed. That has happened on this codebase
# once already: a symlink pointing at its own parent went into a commit, and
# every checkout afterwards failed with ELOOP.
node_modules

# `dist` is NOT here, and that is deliberate too — see PACKAGING.md. This
# package is consumed straight from git, a git dependency gets no
# devDependencies, so there is no `tsc` on the consumer's side to build it with.
# The build is committed because the repository has to BE the artifact.
#
# `bun test` rebuilds it before it runs a single test, so drift shows up as a
# dirty working tree rather than as a consumer quietly compiling against last
# week's contract.
